    "observations": [
        "Both installed browsers show observed props and hook values changing from 0 to 1 without reload in development and minified production.",
        "Minified production component name vo is real runtime metadata, not a replacement fixture name.",
        "Native empty-root panels have no component values; native non-React Components panels show No React detected.",
        "Overlay and standalone matrix verifies the same four unannotated modes, including live standalone values from 1 to 2.",
        "Eight Vite product smoke tests cover desktop, 360px and 420px real standalone layouts and real asset/graph workflows."
    ],
    "limitations": [
        "No Vue UI parity or owner visual approval claimed. Styling remains later issues.",
        "Read-only props/hooks adapter, not completed R06/R07 identity/context/class-state/serialization. Production hook-kind inference is limited; a useState hook may be labeled reducer although its actual value is shown.",
        "Source actions removed until supported; real Fiber picker remains R09. Legacy DOM annotations cannot create a selected Fiber.",
        "Automatic navigation/reconnect and official-extension coexistence remain subsequent issues.",
        "Firefox remote DOM text is inaccessible: exact profile identity, actual native context, passive inspection responses and visually checked native images jointly establish results.",
        "Chrome also opens an unrelated about:blank native inspector whose permission-denied handshake is not evidence of the actual inspected app. Actual app identity is asserted before native model checks.",
        "Fixed-port Firefox prototype captures were excluded after a stale diagnostic browser was discovered. Final captures use a unique port and exact disposable profile assertion.",
        "Earlier negative diagnostic assertions incorrectly expected no native tab. Final checks require the actual native No React detected state with no invented component values.",
        "Development artifacts only, not signed or approved browser-store distribution."
    ]
}
